    Task 50/441: HNSW scan.rs grouped_candidate_rerank_comparison_score reference-pass lift
    
    Lift grouped_candidate_rerank_comparison_score from an unsafe fn
    taking *mut TqScanOpaque to a safe fn taking &mut TqScanOpaque.
    Both callers already had &mut TqScanOpaque in scope and were doing
    the *mut cast purely to thread through the unsafe-fn contract, so
    the new signature avoids the anti-pattern-B-flavoured raw-pointer
    threading entirely.
    
    All five internal scan_opaque_ref/scan_opaque_mut sites collapse to
    direct &mut TqScanOpaque borrows. Two caller-side unsafe { ... }
    wraps stripped (buffer_grouped_graph_result_candidate and
    materialize_graph_result_candidate).
    
